Yes this is thread-safe, since the inner vectors are solely modified by one thread. You can omit the schedule(dynamic) derivative and still be save. This becomes a bit clearer, if you get rid of the inner loop using std::iota . vector<vector<int> > global_vec(10, vector<int>({}));

