double answer1 = myobject.function1();
double answer2 = myobject.function2(); I would like to have those 2 computations run in parallel to save computation time. I've seen that this could be done using openmp, but couldn't figure out how to set it up. The only examples I found were sending the same calculation (i.e. "hello world!" for example) to the different cores and the output was 2 times "hello world!". How can I do it in this situation? I use Windows XP with Visual Studio 2005.

answers.body:
You should look into the sections construct of OpenMP. It works like this: #pragma omp parallel sections
{
   #pragma omp section
   {
      ... section 1 block ...
   }
   #pragma omp section
   {
      ... section 2 block ...
   }
