answers.body:
I get the same problem with ICC but not GCC.  Looks like a bug.  Here is a workaround void pass_vector_by_value2(std::vector<double> p) {
    #pragma omp parallel
    {
        std::vector<double> p_private = p;
        //do sth with p_private      
    }
} On the other hand, in general, I don't pass non-POD by value to functions anyway.  I would use a reference but if you do that you get the error error: ‘p’ has reference type for ‘firstprivate’ The solution to that is the code I posted above anyway.  Pass it by value or by reference and then define a private copy inside the parallel region as I did in the code above.

