Rather than using a pair of nested parallel sections, you can tell OpenMP to "collapse" the nested loops into a single parallel section over the n*m iteration space: #pragma omp parallel for collapse(2)
for (int i{0}; i < n; ++i) {
  for (int j{0}; j < m; ++j) {
    // ...
  }
} This will allow it to divide the work appropriately regardless of the relative values of n and m.

